{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-strictly-perfect}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e26023d3b0a4c1e6f011f919673baae804ea5c25d435aa7a38afd596fb290334", "source_text": "Strictly perfect complexes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:66760bcc11b954d0abdd4b6826e4a36dcd84edbb6346c1ffb85efe48e568cdd2", "unit_id": "tag:08FK:title"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{cohomology-section-strictly-perfect}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ec14f1f7b8ca70d8febf75bb3fc0803b9e3171c510962e620f4e9cc877ee5164", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of\nCohomology, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8f5e55849b16ed4149bcb022c6948a5f3cec9c6917b21919e6b11ad81020673a", "unit_id": "tag:08FK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{E}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}^i$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{E}^i$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0009": "$i$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-strictly-perfect}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d3c9103f58b2b24a899b5f48cdad93e871cf7d15a6a76e0b519b6a258de46d4a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:99e4fa3d1b1f9aa6c363d31ed9f02f33bda1c00b066fa902f3ce7d671e3f4803", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a complex of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nWe say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>strictly perfect<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif <MATH_0005> is zero for all but finitely many <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> is a direct summand of a finite free\n<MATH_0008>-module for all <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd64764c8bcbbfed4604a60aaaee181083c10d60350627bbe90fd9657cc3ad03", "unit_id": "tag:08FL:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{E}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\mathcal{C}/U, \\mathcal{O}_U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-localize-ringed-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9ea28c05392ddcf61e41d0d54bed34e5e2d3c759f2489ff5837ffecb1e74e931", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48ee8e20afa4dc83ef4b74f106c39fbbc20602201ff22b56e5dd43c4ffa148f8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002>. We will often say\n``Let <MATH_0003> be a strictly perfect complex of\n<MATH_0004>-modules'' to mean <MATH_0005> is a strictly perfect\ncomplex of modules on the ringed site <MATH_0006>, see\nModules on Sites, Definition\n<REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d21fb9b15140fa06c8827717018c0248d6be006a241059c59f72b7d104f48b8", "unit_id": "tag:08FK:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cone}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:34f954af2c6dc9dd6cbd6e159119d2bbf001d3ccd710f0579891d14c9b2565e6", "source_text": "The cone on a morphism of strictly perfect complexes is\nstrictly perfect.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0dcd61eb62b03fe8d9a38ae2f16845251ed27b8104e57237dfa123a73dd9b054", "unit_id": "tag:08FM:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0eba86f15471d1581886256b7137dfec39c3ab5a3f6ea3d05d5655c73d0bab69", "source_text": "This is immediate from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:22d564f0a7e0afa0d6e0d815c5b9ddc932cd7bba6994a0f30c2877a93337c6c3", "unit_id": "tag:08FM:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-tensor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb08b53cdd92543e2aaa41780d63986e01266411562e3675554513efd2ec93fa", "source_text": "The total complex associated to the tensor product of two\nstrictly perfect complexes is strictly perfect.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:66baba13494d7020988b6cb0bb3d7d34eec68fbb34bbf9658f99f516a676013e", "unit_id": "tag:09J8:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0eba86f15471d1581886256b7137dfec39c3ab5a3f6ea3d05d5655c73d0bab69", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:09J8:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\mathcal{D}, \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$f^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-strictly-perfect-pullback}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fa7cad5a72ebdba6a4ba613b50da237ed8e8fa80aa76a3f12cb03aab4f64183b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9f9a14a20f71812b60640caf6abdae26790055bff5be93a1e742cf48c33f519a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed topoi. If <MATH_0002> is a strictly\nperfect complex of <MATH_0003>-modules, then\n<MATH_0004> is a strictly perfect complex of\n<MATH_0005>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67b25c00ea066e4e3da8a90b22973666e32bdac59d83166a81f2d155fbb623b1", "unit_id": "tag:08H3:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-global-pullback}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a90771c0b33b2235aa2499c869ed3292c0fcae5305f0ae088e21632ec1f30af4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:805ec63ed145eee665b1905394e566197624c8e323cf495f7f8ea9cb31452475", "source_text": "We have seen in\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthat the pullback of a finite free module is finite free. The functor\n<MATH_0001> is additive functor hence preserves direct summands. The lemma follows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf4db742bbd6fcb4a9d371e88b89efc78150842fd1f244c41af7da06e79dd9b4", "unit_id": "tag:08H3:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{E} \\ar@{..>}[dr] \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{F} \\\\\n& \\mathcal{G} \\ar[u]_p\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0008": "$p$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0010": "$U_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-local-lift-map}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a8db0f60aab18af4828240e2a39378e0a7d554b16f4676f53da3d95efa45350a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b8a1400ab432f32ec0e2104b7fd683017b8c913b1c9a2eba38d208af702fa728", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Let <MATH_0002> be an object of\n<MATH_0003>. Given a solid diagram of <MATH_0004>-modules\n<MATH_0005>\nwith <MATH_0006> a direct summand of a finite free\n<MATH_0007>-module and <MATH_0008> surjective, then there exists a\ncovering <MATH_0009> such that a dotted arrow\nmaking the diagram commute exists over each <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e301b8ff1212ba2369ea1ffcf3462cf3f7fedc40ae18664c242a11136d18f5c2", "unit_id": "tag:08FN:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08FK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{E} = \\mathcal{O}_U^{\\oplus n}$", "MATH_0002": "$n$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{F})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-sheaves-injective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a1d311fed1771814a6bd7fbd74d6eb861b31c60f76433fbccaf186fe447eb9db", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6204e29d005af966178518ad18920c28a3aa1454dfc22fc496e9821f4b09808c", "source_text": "We may assume <MATH_0001> for some <MATH_0002>.\nIn this case finding the dotted arrow is equivalent to lifting the\nimages of the basis elements in <MATH_0003>. This is\nlocally possible by the characterization of surjective maps of\nsheaves (Sites, Section <REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e1511e64680789f13359905be0fd0bbf77b98f6028f0351e15e76e0947d2559", "unit_id": "tag:08FN:proof"}
